WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.243
Healthcare privatization.

00:00:02.193 --> 00:00:04.454
The degradation pipeline.

00:00:04.454 --> 00:00:07.477
Step one: underfund the public system.

00:00:07.477 --> 00:00:11.318
Step two: allow wait times to reach crisis levels.

00:00:11.318 --> 00:00:15.090
Step three: create demand for private alternatives.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.977
Step four: private equity invests in those alternatives.

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:25.988
Step five: the PM who formerly led investment at one of those private equity firms now sets the policy environment.

00:00:25.988 --> 00:00:29.386
This page documents each step from official data.

00:00:29.386 --> 00:00:33.124
Canadian Institute for Health Information wait time data.

00:00:33.124 --> 00:00:35.761
Health Canada staffing statistics.

00:00:35.761 --> 00:00:38.022
Provincial budget documents.

00:00:38.022 --> 00:00:41.261
Corporate filings from healthcare investment firms.

00:00:41.261 --> 00:00:43.874
The pipeline is not hypothetical.

00:00:43.874 --> 00:00:47.329
It is documented, operational, and accelerating.

00:00:47.329 --> 00:00:50.159
The five-step privatization pipeline.

00:00:50.159 --> 00:00:52.999
Each step documented from official data.

00:00:52.999 --> 00:00:55.011
The MAID intersection.

00:00:55.011 --> 00:00:58.897
Where healthcare privatization meets medical assistance in dying.

00:00:58.897 --> 00:01:04.272
When the public healthcare system cannot provide treatment, some patients are offered MAID instead.

00:01:04.272 --> 00:01:06.261
This is documented.

00:01:06.261 --> 00:01:09.715
Veterans seeking mental health support were offered MAID.

00:01:09.715 --> 00:01:14.079
Patients with treatable conditions but long wait times have accessed MAID.

00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:22.704
The economic analysis is documented in the MAID economics page: each MAID death costs the healthcare system eight thousand one hundred and fifty dollars.

00:01:22.704 --> 00:01:27.772
Each year of long-term care costs between fifty and one hundred thousand dollars.

00:01:27.772 --> 00:01:38.954
The financial incentive aligns: MAID reduces the patient population that the degraded public system cannot serve, reducing the visible failure of the system while generating cost savings that benefit the fiscal position.

00:01:38.954 --> 00:01:41.102
The complete architecture.

00:01:41.102 --> 00:01:45.034
Degrade the public system through underfunding and understaffing.

00:01:45.034 --> 00:01:48.795
Allow wait times to create demand for private alternatives.

00:01:48.795 --> 00:01:51.988
Invest in those alternatives through private equity.

00:01:51.988 --> 00:01:56.749
Set policy through political leadership that emerged from those same investment firms.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.806
Reduce system costs through MAID expansion.

00:01:59.806 --> 00:02:02.272
This is not one conspiracy.

00:02:02.272 --> 00:02:16.874
It is multiple documented institutional decisions, each rational in isolation, that together produce a system where public healthcare degrades, private healthcare profits, and the political leadership that connects both faces zero accountability from the oversight bodies documented on this site.
